    "title": "City's Million-Dollar Dump: Dallas Lot Bought for Flood Fix Becomes Trashy Eyesore - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Richard Dawson ,\n9 hours ago A 5.5-acre patch of city-owned land off Manana Drive that Dallas bought in 2008 with bond money has morphed into an illegal dump and a sprawling homeless encampment. Land that was supposed to play a role in an Elm Fork flood-protection plan is now clogged with mattresses, tires, abandoned recreational vehicles and other debris. Neighbors and park advocates say taxpayers are stuck with a pricey tract the city never actually developed. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
